      "level": 2,
      "depth": 1,
      "anchor": "evolution_appendix6_005",
      "text_preview": "In univariate calculus, the local extrema of a function occur when its slope (first derivative) is zero. The multivariate extension is that the gradient vector is zero, so the slope of the function with respect to all variables is zero. A point $ x {e} $ where this occurs is called a stationary or equilibrium point, a…"
